---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout current="/" description="Richard J. Allen is an operations and customer-success leader with experience in SaaS support, process improvement, training, reporting, team leadership, and cross-functional execution.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Operations · Customer Success · Process Improvement · People Leadership</div>
    <h1>Helping people, processes, customers, and operations work better together.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Richard Allen, an operations and customer-success leader based in Oregon. My background combines SaaS/software support, customer experience, team leadership and coaching, process improvement, project coordination, operational reporting, training, supply operations, and change support. I’m strongest in work where teams need structure, performance needs to be measurable, and complex operations need to become clearer and more repeatable.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">View selected work</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Career impact at a glance</div><h2>Work that turns complexity into something usable.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from operations, reporting, SaaS support, and process-improvement work.</p></div>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">100+</span></div><div class="metric-label">SOPs ultimately identified, created, and collected in a year-long OED program, with 25+ legacy procedures inventoried and updated</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">21</span></div><div class="metric-label">people in the documented HawkSoft Customer Service group during Team Lead-era scope</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">400+</span></div><div class="metric-label">workforce position records managed across multiple Oregon Health Authority divisions</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">20+</span></div><div class="metric-label">recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports maintained for leadership</div></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>Where I add value</h2>
    <div class="grid two value-grid">
      <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">01</div><h3>Operations & people leadership</h3><p>People management, coaching, workflow coverage, quality review, hiring and performance, operational reporting, escalations, onboarding, and cross-functional coordination. Earlier warehouse-management experience adds supply, inventory, driver, and mixed-workforce leadership.</p><a href="/operations-leadership/">Operations & leadership →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">02</div><h3>Customer success & SaaS support</h3><p>Customer relationships, technical support leadership, escalations, training, software adoption, migrations, customer-journey work, release support, and customer-experience improvement.</p><a href="/customer-success/">Customer success experience →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">03</div><h3>Process improvement & documentation</h3><p>Led/co-led a year-long SOP modernization and governance program across roughly 10 functional groups, inventorying and updating 25+ legacy procedures and centralizing a library that ultimately identified, created, and collected 100+ SOPs.</p><a href="/process-improvement/">Process improvement work →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">04</div><h3>Implementation & enablement</h3><p>Customer migrations, major software-change readiness, advance communication, launch coverage, functional testing, product documentation, training, onboarding, and coordination between technical and customer-facing teams.</p><a href="/implementation-enablement/">Implementation & enablement →</a></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section project-work-home"><div class="container">
    <div class="project-teaser">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow light">Also available for selected project work</div>
        <h2>Need an important process documented clearly?</h2>
        <p>I take on selected short-term projects involving SOP creation and cleanup, workflow documentation, training/onboarding guides, support-operations procedures, and documentation governance. This remains a secondary project-work lane alongside my primary search for the right long-term role.</p>
        <div class="service-chips"><span>SOPs</span><span>Workflow documentation</span><span>Training guides</span><span>Support procedures</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/project-work/">View project services</a><a class="text-link-light" href="/contact/">Discuss a project →</a></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="callout"><strong>Leadership beyond the workplace.</strong> Volunteer hospital chaplaincy, community administration, emergency-preparedness coordination, mentoring, and service work reinforce the same habits I value professionally: listening, organizing, communicating clearly, and helping people move through real-world needs. <a href="/community-leadership/">See community & volunteer leadership →</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
